    - target: {fileID: 1846833183091735543, guid: 5aa8f79cd6416fd4ea3f09ac4a61ebc3, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "This mode is more expensive (in terms of both speed and texture memory
        usage) than just using the Camera Opaque Texture, as you must copy a second
        screen texture during the rendering loop. \n\nHowever, it makes some effects
        possible which would otherwise be impossible. Be aware that you will still
        not be able to see any objects which use Camera Transparent Texture when
        viewed through an object using Camera Transparent Texture.\n\nIf you don't
        see a difference between the two spheres here, make sure the camera is using
        the correct Renderer Data and you have set up the Camera Transparent Texture
        as described."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
